{
  "sim_type": "excel",
  "title": "Banking Sector Revenue Trends — Pivot-Equivalent Cross-Tab",
  "scenario": "Your desk has received quarterly consolidated financials for ten major Indian banks (FY25–FY26, Q1–Q4). The head of research needs sector-wide revenue summaries, margin performance by quarter, and top performers identified — fast. Instead of building a live PivotTable (which the auto-grader cannot verify), you will replicate the pivot's exact output using SUMIFS and INDEX-MATCH formulas, so every number is auditable and you master the logic behind the drag.",
  "instructions": "Build a cross-tabular summary equivalent to a PivotTable: use SUMIFS to compute total revenue by bank and quarter; calculate average margin by quarter; identify the highest-revenue bank per quarter using INDEX-MATCH; and produce a sector-wide grand total. Each formula must reference the Data sheet and stand alone for audit.",
  "learning_objective": "Compute multi-dimensional summaries (revenue by bank and time, margin trends, top performers) using SUMIFS and INDEX-MATCH, replicating PivotTable logic without the GUI — so you understand the architecture pivots hide and can audit any summary number to its source row.",
  "hints": [
    "SUMIFS syntax: =SUMIFS(sum_range, criteria_range1, criteria1, criteria_range2, criteria2, …). For Q1 revenue from HDFC, use the bank and quarter columns as your criteria ranges.",
    "To find the highest-revenue bank in Q1, use INDEX(bank_names, MATCH(MAX(sumifs_array), sumifs_array, 0)) — but you'll need to build the sumifs array first (one SUMIFS per bank), or use a simpler approach: sort the data mentally and verify by hand.",
    "Grand Total = SUM of all quarterly revenue across all banks. A single SUMIFS with no bank criterion (only summing the entire Revenue column) will give you the total. Margin average per quarter = AVERAGEIF(Quarter_column, quarter_value, Margin_column)."
  ],
